BLE Clipboard is an independent, unofficial project for Flipper Zero.
It is not affiliated with Flipper Devices, Apple, Microsoft, or Homebrew.

The Flipper application uses the public Flipper Zero firmware SDK and its
Bluetooth, GUI, storage, and USB HID APIs, maintained by Flipper Devices Inc.
and contributors: https://github.com/flipperdevices/flipperzero-firmware

Source code in this repository is licensed under GPL-3.0-only; see LICENSE.
The SDK, firmware, Apple frameworks, and Homebrew retain their own licenses.

Version 0.3.0 and later use this project's own BLE transport, typed binary macro format,
program validator and USB execution state machine. It does not bundle another
project's typing engine or a third-party script interpreter.

The built-in macOS Turkish-Q mapping uses standard USB HID usages and was
checked against Apple's installed keyboard translation through UCKeyTranslate.
No Apple keyboard layout binary or private framework is redistributed.

The macOS icon was generated using OpenAI image generation and adapted into
Apple's ICNS sizes using sips and iconutil. See docs/ARTWORK.md.

Catalog screenshots are unmodified qFlipper exports. The optional host preview
adapter uses official firmware 1.5.1 u8g2/font/button resources. Firmware GUI
behavior is GPL-3.0 licensed; u8g2 retains its upstream BSD license and font
notices. No firmware library or font source is vendored by the adapter. See the
provenance under BluetoothClipboard/screenshots and the firmware source above.

The Windows companion uses Python, Tcl/Tk, Bleak, PyWinRT and regex. Windows
packages include their actual runtime license texts and the PyInstaller
bootloader/Inno Setup notices in THIRD-PARTY.txt; the same text is a separate
WINDOWS-THIRD-PARTY.txt release asset. Windows screenshots are genuine offline
CI renders with synthetic libraries and Bluetooth/output disabled, not device
captures. See BLEClipboardWindows/README.md and docs/ARTWORK.md.
